  "articleBody": "When a severe storm hits DFW, it can leave your roof in a state of uncertainty. Knowing what to do immediately afterward can prevent further damage and help with any potential insurance claims. Your first priority should always be safety, so make sure to check for obvious hazards before getting too close to the property. Once it's safe to assess, quick and thorough action is key to protecting your home and investment.\n\n**Common Mistakes to Avoid**\nIt’s tempting to start cleaning up right away, but discarding damaged items before documenting them can cause issues. Don't enter unsafe structures or climb a visibly compromised roof. And try not to make permanent repairs until your insurer has had a chance to inspect, as this can weaken your documentation. Also, ensure you label any photos or videos by room or specific damage location for clarity.\n\nAfter ensuring safety, your next step should be documenting everything. Take detailed photos and videos of all affected areas, inside and out. Note the date of the storm and the locations of damage. Separate damaged items from undamaged ones. This visual evidence is crucial for communicating the extent of the storm's impact. If you're unsure, or if there are structural concerns, bringing in a professional for an emergency storm damage assessment is smart. They can help identify hidden issues and provide a clear report.\n\nDon't forget to report the damage to your insurer according to your policy's guidelines. The sooner they know, the better. A professional assessment report can give you a clear, objective picture of the damage, guiding your next steps for repair or replacement.\n\nFor a clear emergency storm damage assessment in DFW, contact Discounted Roofing Co. today.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}